  <!-- SECTION 1: The Security Challenge -->
  <section id="problem-statement" class="case-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span>01 / MOTIVATION & OBJECTIVES</span>
      <span class="evidence-tag">CHALLENGE & STRATEGY</span>
    </div>
    <h2>Moving from Reactive Security to Shift-Left Governance</h2>
    <p>
      In conventional CI/CD implementations, security checks are either omitted entirely, delegated to asynchronous weekly scans, or gated by static, high-privilege AWS credentials stored indefinitely in GitHub Secrets. When vulnerabilities reach production, remediation costs increase exponentially, and compromised CI runner credentials frequently lead to total AWS account takeovers.
    </p>

    <div class="evidence-box">
      <div class="evidence-title">CORE SECURITY ARCHITECTURE OBJECTIVES</div>
      <ul style="margin: 10px 0; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <li><strong>Eliminate Credential Theft Risk:</strong> Eliminate all long-lived AWS IAM Access Keys from GitHub repository secrets using native OpenID Connect (OIDC) web identity federation.</li>
        <li><strong>Automated Hard Quality Gates:</strong> Reject pull requests automatically if secrets are leaked, raw SQL concatenation is introduced, high-severity CVEs exist in dependencies, or Terraform breaches CIS benchmarks.</li>
        <li><strong>Dynamic Security Validation (DAST):</strong> Crawl and probe active ephemeral containers using OWASP ZAP to catch runtime misconfigurations (missing anti-clickjacking headers, improper cache policies) prior to production deployment.</li>
        <li><strong>Defense-in-Depth Container Runtime:</strong> Build multi-stage Alpine images executing strictly as unprivileged user <code>UID: 10001</code> with embedded liveness probes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

